invalid type: string "9. Conclusion and Future Research\nDeep-sea bioluminescence continues to offer key insights for biological imaging, optogenetics, and\nmarine ecology. As modern submersibles and optical sensors expand human observation into the lower\nbathypelagic and abyssopelagic zones, further structural variations of photic regulation are expected to\nbe unveiled.", expected a booleanÿÿÿÿ